WEBVTT

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:12.280
Tea time, everyone!

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:15.740
Okay, Sissy!

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:23.160
Here you go. It's hot, so be careful.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.670
Okay!

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.380
I don't taste anything, Sissy.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.510
I don't, either.

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:33.760
It's really weak.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.680
Sorry, children. We don't 
have that much tea left.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.470
We have to use it sparingly.

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:42.730
Sissy, why do we have tea every day?

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:48.190
Tea time is a very important time when 
we all get to relax with each other.

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:51.820
If you're having fun, it warms 
up your hearts even more,

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:54.900
and if you're sad, 
it'll help calm your hearts.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.110
Right, Father?

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.740
Yes. Remembering to relax 
is always important.

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:02.240
So remember to treasure 
these moments, children.

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:04.200
Okay!

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:40.010
The Dragon's Daughter

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:43.890
Let's see. Wheat, potatoes, and tea...

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:49.310
I'm sorry. This is all we have.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:52.270
No, thank you for always accommodating us.

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:53.980
I don't know what I'm gonna do...

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:55.860
Everything's getting more expensive.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:59.610
It's wartime. There's not 
much we can do about it.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:05.280
I wonder if this will be 
enough for this month...

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.910
We can do something about the rest.

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:12.580
I know, Schaal. I can finally 
teach you how to hunt.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:14.040
Hunt? Me?!

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.170
Let's go right now!

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:20.010
Today? Right now? But I'm not ready...

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:18.760
Sissy!

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.210
Father!

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:20.010
Welcome back!

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:24.050
Right there, Sissy!

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:25.180
Hurry, hurry!

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:26.470
W-Wait!

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:29.680
Slowly... Stay calm.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:32.520
Make sure you're aiming...

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:35.520
Okay, now.

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:37.150
Fire.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:42.660
Sissy, hurry!

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:43.820
It's gonna get away!

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:47.330
It got away...

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:48.240
Aw, man!

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:50.450
What are you doing, Sissy?

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:54.460
The deer turned into mushrooms...

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:56.130
That's perfectly fine.

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:59.590
I love your mushroom soup, Schaal.

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:00.420
Me, too!

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:01.470
It's so yummy.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:02.800
I like it, too.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:05.720
I wanted some venison soup.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:08.680
Don't feel bad.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:11.390
Hunting means taking the 
life of a living creature.

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:13.390
It's not such a simple thing to do.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:19.360
But if the war keeps going and 
we run out of food, then...

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:24.200
Don't worry. You're a strong girl.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:27.780
When the time comes for you to pull the 
trigger, I know you'll be able to do it.

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:30.790
Daddy, Sissy.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:33.500
We have guests.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:38.090
What? Soldiers?

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:41.420
Why? What would they want here?

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:55.390
Sissy.

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:56.770
I'm hungry.

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:58.270
The soup's gonna get cold.

00:04:58.270 --> 00:04:58.980
You're right...

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:01.280
I guess we can start eating.

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:02.440
Okay!

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:04.650
Let's eat!

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:17.120
That took a while.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:18.750
It did. I'm sorry.

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:20.750
How are the kids?

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.670
They fell asleep.

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:23.760
I see...

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:26.930
Here you go.

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:27.890
Thanks.

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:39.230
I have to go off to the war.

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:40.060
What?

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:44.440
I leave at the beginning of next week. 
I'll tell the children tomorrow...

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:45.650
Wait!

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:49.570
Why do you have to fight in the war? 
You're not a soldier!

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:53.540
Apparently, there's something 
unique about me.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:57.040
That doesn't matter! 
You should've just said no!

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:02.630
They promised that the town and this 
orphanage will receive funding if I go.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.920
The kids will be able to 
eat their fill every day.

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:12.010
It doesn't matter if we don't have 
much food! I want to be with you!

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:14.970
I'm sure the kids feel the same way!

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:19.480
If you go to the war and something happens...

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:29.910
Schaal, I didn't decide to go 
to the war just for the money.

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:33.030
I have the power to help end this war

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:37.500
and make sure that you and the other 
kids can live happily in the future.

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:41.080
This is my time to pull the trigger.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:42.920
I hope you'll understand.

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:52.930
Make sure you kids behave.

00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:52.090
Don't go, Daddy!

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:53.760
Do your best, Daddy!

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:54.180
We'll be good.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:54.180
Daddy!

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.770
Leave the children to us.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:57.850
Be careful.

00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:02.940
I will. I promise to end this war 
with this special power I have.

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:04.610
Father...

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:06.860
Here.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:08.650
What's this?

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.200
Please come home safe...

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:22.170
See you soon! We believe in you!

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:28.550
Thank you. I'm off now.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:46.860
This is Special Private 
John William Bancroft.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:51.070
We return this to you.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.050
Father...

00:08:15.550 --> 00:08:16.930
It's Father...

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:19.310
Welcome home.

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:25.900
He looks different now, 
but he's still our father.

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:30.730
Welcome home, Daddy...

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:35.820
Daddy!

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:36.280
Welcome home!

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:37.700
You look so cool!

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:40.080
You have wings! Can you fly?

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:39.450
We missed you!

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:40.080
Don't ever leave us again!

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:50.090
Go, Daddy!

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:51.590
Wow!

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:55.970
Over here, too!

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:57.470
Wow!

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:18.990
Here you go.

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:22.750
Here's your mutton and beef for the day.

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:24.580
Thank you very much.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:26.290
Are you all right, Schaal?

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:26.960
Huh?

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:28.580
This is what you get every day.

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:31.550
Isn't it tough to survive on just 
the government's funding?

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:32.920
Yes.

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:38.300
Will is this town's hero. 
We'll do everything we can to help.

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:41.010
So don't worry about a thing.

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:42.260
Thank you.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:49.020
I have to cut expenses even more...

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:52.780
Guess we won't be able 
to buy tea anymore.

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:00.700
What in the world?

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:03.790
What?

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:04.700
What is that?

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:05.540
Is it a wolf?

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:14.000
Father!

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:22.180
Father?

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:31.020
More of my cows were killed.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:33.070
That's ten now.

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:35.320
They were torn to pieces.

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:38.150
Are you suspecting my father?

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:41.030
He's screaming more often at night,

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:45.410
and I hear that you haven't been able 
to get enough food for a while now.

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:50.000
We're very grateful to Will. We're not 
suspecting him because we want to.

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:51.330
But...

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.630
We need him to wear this.

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:58.170
No... My father is human!

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:00.380
This is a request from the whole town.

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:05.430
Please understand... We thought we could 
prove Will's innocence if he'd wear this.

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:09.770
I understand.

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:12.350
Also, Schaal...

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:14.940
About the children...

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:19.570
I don't wanna go!

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:21.410
Sissy!

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:24.030
Why do we have to go?

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:25.370
No!

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:28.540
Sissy!

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:31.080
Children...

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:36.840
Schaal, this is what's best for them.

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:40.010
So far, we've only lost 
some cows, but what if...

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:41.760
It'll be too late if we wait 
until something happens.

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:42.930
You understand, don't you?

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:58.820
Everyone's gone...

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:07.870
Say, Father... Why don't we go 
somewhere far away together?

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:13.790
We can build a house in the 
forest and live there together.

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:15.960
Together forever...

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:26.470
Father?

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:39.860
Huh? What's going on?!

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:43.740
Father!

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:51.620
Father!

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:26.610
N... No...

00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:30.490
No...

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:33.700
Why?

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:48.550
Father...

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:51.260
Don't leave me alone.

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:54.220
Father! Father!

00:13:57.390 --> 00:14:02.320
Father, no! Father!

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:17.620
<i>Father...</i>

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:35.470
Why was my father...

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:46.530
He killed my father...

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:59.330
<i>The man in the white coat...</i>

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:02.540
<i>He won't get away with this.</i>

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:46.800
He's not here, either.

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:53.010
<i>Father...</i>

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:06.320
What the...

00:16:06.320 --> 00:16:07.150
A girl?

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:08.360
Is that a real rifle?

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:09.990
I found you!

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:13.950
The man in the white coat!

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:17.490
<i>Father...</i>

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:26.710
<i>Give me strength!</i>

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:41.930
Did I get him?

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:50.110
Ow...

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:54.410
Hey... He's not hurt?

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:56.410
How is he okay?

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:03.000
No! Let me go! Let go!

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.000
What the hell?

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:05.040
Who were they?

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:07.000
He just ran off with the one who shot him.

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:10.630
Who are you?

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:14.170
My name is Nancy Schaal Bancroft.

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:16.510
I'm John William Bancroft's daughter!

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:21.100
I see... You're Will's...

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:24.440
How are you alive?! I know I hit you!

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:27.270
This isn't enough to kill us.

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:28.360
Huh?

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:29.730
I-It's Danny!

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:31.070
Danny's back!

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:31.780
There he is.

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:32.820
Get the kids inside the house!

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:34.360
Stay here if you don't want to die.

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:34.360
Hide! It's dangerous!

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:37.410
You're just saying that so you can run away!

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:38.700
Who in the world is here?!

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:42.160
Another Incarnate,
 just like Will and myself.

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:48.670
W-Welcome home, Danny.

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:50.840
I'm home, Mom.

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:53.630
Guys, look at how much I got.

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:57.220
If you sell all of this, 
the town will really prosper.

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:02.470
O-Of course, Danny... Thank you so much.

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:07.650
There have been several instances

00:18:07.650 --> 00:18:10.400
of wagons being attacked
 on the road nearby.

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:16.610
Apparently, the drivers and merchants were 
all killed, crushed by a large object.

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:19.990
You did it, didn't you, Danny?

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:22.240
Who are you?

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:25.620
Danny, no! Please don't!

00:18:23.990 --> 00:18:25.410
No, Mrs. Price!

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:25.950
It's dangerous! Stay back!

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:28.040
Do you remember, Danny?

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:30.790
The oath we made that day?

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:34.630
Those who have lost their souls 
shall be slain by their own.

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:37.550
Captain...

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:42.140
Wait!

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:44.350
Are you going to kill him, too?

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:45.890
Just like you killed my father?

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:48.850
Did you actually see him 
attack any wagons?

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:51.110
Are you sure he actually—

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:52.400
I asked them nicely to give me stuff...

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:58.200
Because if they gave me money or jewels, 
everyone in the town would be happy...

00:18:58.570 --> 00:19:00.910
But they wouldn't give me any.

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:04.330
That's why I killed them!

00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:07.330
Get back!

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:12.460
I'm going to give my mom an easy life!

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:15.090
I'm going to make everyone happy!

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:16.460
Why...

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:19.430
I'll kill you! I'll kill you! 
I'll kill you! I'll kill you!

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:17.550
You can't help him.

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:19.430
There's no stopping him now.

00:19:19.430 --> 00:19:24.300
I'll kill anyone who gets in 
my way! Even you, Captain!

00:19:24.810 --> 00:19:27.730
You've become pretty selfish, Danny.

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:50.000
Daniel Price...

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:52.620
You were once a kind man.

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:58.010
My town is so poor, we can 
barely even drink coffee.

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:03.720
But if I fight, everyone will 
be able to live better lives.

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:06.350
That makes me so happy!

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:12.270
I did... what I did... for everyone...

00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:13.730
Danny...

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:16.820
Danny! Danny!

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:22.360
Captain...

00:20:23.410 --> 00:20:25.370
Please, tell me...

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:26.780
Should I...

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:30.620
Should we have...

00:20:30.620 --> 00:20:34.710
just died as gods on that battlefield?

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:38.550
Danny, I'm sorry.

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:44.720
Danny!

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:48.930
Danny... Please wake up, Danny...

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:52.230
Danny...

00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:56.520
Are you going to go kill 
more of your comrades?

00:20:57.190 --> 00:20:59.780
We swore an oath.

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:03.820
Why?! The war's over now!

00:21:04.530 --> 00:21:07.070
But it's not over... None of it.

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:11.500
None of us were able to finish it.

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:14.000
What do you mean?

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:17.130
What happened to the Incarnates squad?

00:21:17.490 --> 00:21:21.210
You killed my father before 
I could find anything out!

00:21:21.660 --> 00:21:23.050
Tell me, please!

00:21:39.200 --> 00:21:40.480
In that case...

00:21:41.010 --> 00:21:43.110
I'm going with you!

00:21:44.600 --> 00:21:49.990
I'm going to see why my father 
had to die with my own eyes!

00:23:25.500 --> 00:23:26.920
My name is Liza.

00:23:26.920 --> 00:23:28.670
I support Hank.

00:23:28.670 --> 00:23:29.550
A fortress.

00:23:29.550 --> 00:23:30.680
A fortress?

00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:32.510
A girl... eh?

00:23:33.550 --> 00:23:35.460
You're the one who taught me that

00:23:35.460 --> 00:23:38.140
the way to overcome fear 
is to always be prepared!

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:40.640
The Minotaur's Fortress
